    "summary": "Atlatl, spear-thrower made of wood, bone, bead (glass). Short over all, dagger shaped in outline, the handle is carved simply to fit the right hand with a flat rectangular  bone finger peg inserted at the handle, and an index finger socket cut centrally.Spear shaft groove is terminated by an ivory spur, this side coloured red, though the tint is much faded. The opposite side was probably coloured black, with bevelled sides rising to a surface decorated with two beads decorated blue and white.",
